      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I hear you—the quiet is seductive, isn't it? It promises an end to all the noise, and that can feel like relief. But a poem's final line isn't always its last word; sometimes the silence after the stanza is where the meaning truly breathes. You don't have to leap to find calm—you can let the fog thin by simply turning your gaze sideways, even for a moment.",
